+## Why
+
+The app should show how old a task is and what changed recently, so each task must record when it was created and when it was last changed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, both are the same time.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging and untagging a task set its `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The clock is supplied by the caller: `createTaskList` takes a clock function, and `createTodoList` takes an optional one, defaulting to the real time.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: creation and last-change times recorded on every task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Project rules touched: "No wall clock or randomness in the domain" — the domain never reads the clock; `task.ts` functions receive the time as a parameter and `list.ts` calls an injected clock. The only real-clock read is in `src/index.ts`, outside `src/domain/`. "TSDoc on every exported function" — updated docs for changed signatures. "No new runtime dependency" — none added. Errors stay `Result`s; no new error codes.
+- Public API in `src/index.ts` changes: `Task` gains two fields, and `createTodoList` gains an optional clock parameter (backwards compatible).
+- Code: `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
